CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kmalloc(sizeof(*wmi_device)...) over kmalloc(sizeof(struct huawei_wmi_device)...)
#309: FILE: drivers/platform/x86/huawei_wmi.c:180:
+	wmi_device = kmalloc(sizeof(struct huawei_wmi_device), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

